From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 15:50:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] thunderbolt: nhi: Keep a stopped polling ring masked

A ring in polling mode masks its interrupt when it calls ->start_poll()
and expects the user to unmask it with tb_ring_poll_complete(). If the
ring has been stopped in the meantime, tb_ring_stop() has already
disabled its interrupt, and tb_ring_poll_complete() unmasks it again
for a ring that is no longer running. When the NHI is going away the
host interface registers should not be touched at all.

Only unmask the interrupt when the ring is still running and the NHI is
not going away. Both are checked under the NHI and ring locks, which
tb_ring_stop() also holds.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.c b/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.c
index ce71e79d083..7dff7f41fc8 100644
--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.c
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/nhi.c
@@ -419,7 +419,7 @@ static void __ring_interrupt(struct tb_ring *ring)
  * @ring: Ring to re-start the interrupt
  *
  * This will re-start (unmask) the ring interrupt once the user is done
- * with polling.
+ * with polling, provided the ring is still running and the NHI is not going away.
  */
 void tb_ring_poll_complete(struct tb_ring *ring)
 {
@@ -427,7 +427,7 @@ void tb_ring_poll_complete(struct tb_ring *ring)
 
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&ring->nhi->lock, flags);
 	spin_lock(&ring->lock);
-	if (ring->start_poll)
+	if (ring->start_poll && ring->running && !ring->nhi->going_away)
 		__ring_interrupt_mask(ring, false);
 	spin_unlock(&ring->lock);
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&ring->nhi->lock, flags);
-- 
